 Also called: 3D Texture Mipmap Generation, Compute Shader Mipmap Generation, Volume Mipmapping
 ## Overview
-Mipmap generation creates a hierarchy of downscaled volume data representations to enable multi-resolution rendering and faster traversal [S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of aliasing and performance degradation when viewing high-resolution volumes from a distance or at varying scales [S4, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from siblings like [VoxelGrid Down Sample](1014-voxelgrid-down-sample.md) by explicitly managing the creation of a full mip-chain via compute shaders or specific filtering modes (Average, Halton) rather than simple grid reduction, and differs from [Streaming MIP Implementation (Basic)](1803-streaming-mip-implementation-basic.md) by focusing on the static generation of the hierarchy rather than the streaming of levels [G].
